          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_3zyzVG": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "row_open": false,
            "heading": "Can Parkmore products help with Cushing’s (PPID) in horses?",
            "icon": "storefront",
            "image_width": 20,
            "row_heading_tag": "h3",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes—while we don’t claim to “cure” Cushing’s, we’ve had excellent results helping horses <strong>manage the symptoms</strong> and stay more comfortable using our natural support system.</p><p>For horses with Cushing’s, we recommend the <strong>Parkmore Cushing’s Support Kit</strong>, which includes:</p><ul><li> <strong>Detox</strong> – to clear toxins and support the liver and gut, making the body more receptive to healing.</li><li> <strong>SVMS (Special Vitamin Mineral Supplement)</strong> – to restore nutritional balance, especially when absorption is impaired.</li><li> <strong>Immune Support</strong> – critical for horses whose immune systems are weakened by PPID.</li><li> <strong>Herbal Infusion (HI)</strong> – especially useful for supporting the endocrine system and metabolic health.</li></ul><p>Together, these products help improve coat condition, energy levels, digestion, and overall resilience. Many customers also report better hoof health, reduced seasonal flare-ups, and more manageable weight.</p><p><strong>Important:</strong> Always work alongside your vet when managing Cushing’s, especially if your horse is on medications like Pergolide.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "content_embed": "",
            "button_text_size": "t3",
            "button_label_1": "",
            "button_link_1": "/",
            "button_style_1": "primary",
