        "collapsible_row_UVzCqe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "row_open": false,
            "heading": "Can Parkmore products help with EPM?",
            "icon": "storefront",
            "image_width": 20,
            "row_heading_tag": "h3",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes—<strong>as part of a post-treatment recovery plan</strong>, Parkmore products can be incredibly helpful.</p><p>EPM drains the horse’s system. Even after medication clears the protozoa, you’re often left with a weak, depleted horse—poor coordination, low energy, muscle loss, and a compromised immune system.</p><p>Our <strong>Parkmore EPM Recovery Protocol</strong> supports the nervous system, rebuilds strength, and helps reduce the risk of relapse. It includes:</p><ul><li> <strong>Detox</strong> – to flush lingering toxins and support gut health, especially after heavy medication.</li><li> <strong>SVMS (Special Vitamin Mineral Supplement)</strong> – for cellular repair, nervous system support, and muscle rebuilding.</li><li> <strong>Immune Support</strong> – yeast-based nucleotides to repair immune function and promote regeneration.</li><li> <strong>Herbal Infusion (HI)</strong> – targeted herbs to support blood flow, circulation, and nerve tissue.</li></ul><p><strong>No topical products are needed</strong> unless the horse has developed <strong>skin problems, pressure sores, or secondary infections</strong>—in which case, the <strong>Botanica Herbal Cream and Wash</strong> can be used as needed.</p><p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> EPM treatment should always be led by your vet. Our products are best used as part of a <strong>rehab and long-term recovery</strong> plan.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "content_embed": "",
