        "collapsible_row_h64wyh": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "row_open": false,
            "heading": "Can Parkmore Immune Support help my horse breathe better during cross-country?",
            "icon": "storefront",
            "image_width": 20,
            "row_heading_tag": "h3",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes—especially if your horse struggles with <strong>inflammation, seasonal allergies, or respiratory fatigue</strong> during intense work like galloping, jumping, or hauling across country.</p><p>Parkmore Immune Support isn’t a “breathe-easy” powder or bronchodilator—but it works at a <strong>deeper level</strong> by supporting the <strong>body’s ability to heal, repair, and stay resilient under pressure.</strong></p><p>Here’s how it helps your horse breathe better:</p><ul><li> <strong>Reduces inflammation</strong> at the cellular level—especially in the lungs and upper airway</li><li> <strong>Improves immune resilience</strong>, so the horse is less reactive to pollen, dust, or mold</li><li> <strong>Accelerates cellular repair</strong>, which is critical after heavy work or travel</li><li> <strong>Supports recovery</strong>, helping prevent post-run fatigue, sore lungs, or delayed bounce-back</li></ul><p>In other words, it keeps the <strong>engine running clean</strong>—so the lungs don’t get bogged down by immune overreaction or cellular stress.</p><p>It’s brilliant for:</p><ul><li>Horses with mild heaves or exercise-induced coughing</li><li>Horses recovering from respiratory infections</li><li>Competition horses prone to fatigue, tight breathing, or slower recovery</li></ul>",
            "page": "",
