        "collapsible_row_atEQfc": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "row_open": false,
            "heading": "What makes Parkmore's Steam Activated Charcoal so Special?",
            "icon": "airplane",
            "image_width": 20,
            "row_heading_tag": "h3",
            "row_content": "<p>Most people think charcoal is just burnt wood. But <strong>steam-activated hardwood charcoal</strong> is on another level entirely.</p><p>Here’s why:</p><h5> <strong>1. It’s Steam-Activated, Not Just Burned</strong></h5><ul><li>The steam activation process <strong>superheats the charcoal in the presence of water vapor</strong>, creating a massive <strong>network of microscopic pores</strong>.</li><li>This gives it an <strong>incredible surface area</strong>—just 1 gram can have over <strong>3,000 m² of surface area</strong>.</li><li>That means more places to <strong>bind toxins, gases, pathogens, heavy metals</strong>, and allergens inside the gut.</li></ul><h5> <strong>2. It’s Made from a Specific Blend of Four Hardwoods</strong></h5><ul><li>Not all wood is equal—hardwood charcoal is <strong>cleaner, more consistent</strong>, and burns longer without impurities.</li><li>The Parkmore blend ensures <strong>reliable binding strength</strong> with <strong>no chemical residues</strong>—just pure detox power.</li></ul><h5> <strong>3. It Binds Without Stripping</strong></h5><ul><li>Steam-activated charcoal doesn’t just grab <em>everything</em> like some cheap binders do.</li><li>It has a <strong>high affinity for toxins and unwanted substances</strong>, while <strong>leaving nutrients alone</strong>—which is critical when you're pairing it with SVMS or HI.</li></ul>",
            "page": "",
            "content_embed": "",
